WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.680
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:11.040
Today we are going to have a look at how&nbsp;
Photoshop just got transformed by the generative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.060
AI revolution. And more. Previously, if we had an&nbsp;
image with an object that we wanted to cut out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.920
but in the meantime, also fill in&nbsp;
the gap with sensible information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:30.060
we could use the content-aware fill feature, and&nbsp;
then, this happens. It has done a passable job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.700
and a little fiddling with the parameters&nbsp;
probably yields an okay solution. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:42.120
can we do even better? Well, through the&nbsp;
power of the papers, yes, now we can!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:48.840
Now, experiment number one. Let’s try the new&nbsp;
generative fill feature where we can add a text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:57.180
prompt, and it shall be filled with exactly&nbsp;
that. So that is a wooden table, little AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:04.260
please fill in a wooden table. Wait a minute.&nbsp;
That is not exactly what I was thinking about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:11.340
but perhaps it did exactly what it was asked.&nbsp;
That is a wooden table, can’t argue with that.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:19.020
Alright, experiment two, this one was a sharp&nbsp;
object in focus, but can it deal with blurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:25.200
objects in the background. Let’s change&nbsp;
this bottle to a flower pot. Does it know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.980
how this needs to be done? Will it be out&nbsp;
of focus? That is an excellent solution,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:37.680
great job! I like that we can choose&nbsp;
from several different variants.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:44.400
Now, experiment number three. I am a light&nbsp;
transport researcher by trade, so I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.640
love to see some caustics, that is, light&nbsp;
refracted through the glass here on the table.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:58.380
And…ouch. Okay, this one is a little rough&nbsp;
around the edges at the moment. Although if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.220
we are looking for reflections,&nbsp;
it can do that reasonably well.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.800
Now, experiment number four. When trying&nbsp;
this on not just some small thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:13.860
but on higher quality images, created with&nbsp;
some of the best generative AIs out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:19.500
the quality differences are apparent.&nbsp;
This will not always be able to keep up.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:27.240
Experiment five. This is going to be very&nbsp;
interesting and relevant. It can do not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:35.280
generative inpainting, but outpainting as well.&nbsp;
Oh yes, if we say that we wish to extend an image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:42.420
outwards, it can do that really well in this case.&nbsp;
I don’t see any seams, or in other words, I don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:49.380
see the traces of the algorithm anywhere. If I was&nbsp;
shown this image, I would not be able to tell that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:54.780
some wizardry was going on. Others also seemed&nbsp;
to get really good results with this already.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:01.320
However, don’t take these results and flaws&nbsp;
for granted, these models are improving at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.900
an incredibly rapid pace. For instance, a new&nbsp;
paper describes a technique that is capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:13.980
of something even more incredible. And that is,&nbsp;
magically changing the posture, proportions and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:21.060
the pose of already existing images. This is&nbsp;
incredible. And do you know what is even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:27.240
incredible? You are not going to believe this&nbsp;
- the paper has only been out for a few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.600
and an unofficial implementation of it already&nbsp;
exists, which means that with a little technical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:39.540
expertise, you can already try it yourself.&nbsp;
The link is available in the video description.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:45.900
And get this, there are even two new&nbsp;
techniques for generating images without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:53.100
even writing a text prompt. How is that even&nbsp;
possible? Well, have a look at this. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:58.020
we just drop in an image, and it&nbsp;
generates beautiful variants for it.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:04.440
But, we are not done yet. Not even close.&nbsp;
If we a looking for a bit more control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.920
but we still don’t want to enter a text prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:15.060
which basically sounds almost impossible, well,&nbsp;
we have another new tool. Dear Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:20.520
have a look at this prompt-free diffusion&nbsp;
paper. Yes, this generates images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:28.020
